{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ModelsOfQous.SymmetricPointChannelCollapse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ModelsOfQous.SymmetricPointChannelCollapse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Invertible.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.symmetric_point_channel_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.symmetric_point_channel_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/symmetric-point-channel-collapse.lean#L28-L47","doc":"**Channel collapse at the symmetric point.**  For an involutive unit\n(`s² = 1`) in a commutative ring in which `2` is invertible, the inverse\ncoincides with the element and the averaged channel `(s + s⁻¹)/2`\ncollapses onto it.  This is the algebraic core of the `q = 1`\ndegeneration of the inter-nucleon channel assignments `σ`, `σ⁻¹`,\n`(σ + σ⁻¹)/2`.\n\nBase ring (§7c): `[CommRing R]` with `s : Rˣ` and `[Invertible (2 : R)]`\nin place of the former `[Field R]` with `s ≠ 0` implicit and `(2 : R) ≠ 0`\n— an element with `s² = 1` *is* a unit, and the only division used is by\n`2`.  A field of characteristic `≠ 2` is the special case\n(`invertibleOfNonzero`); `ℤ[1/2][q^{±1}]` is another. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:symmetric-point-channel-collapse","label":"prop:symmetric-point-channel-collapse","md":"quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/symmetric-point-channel-collapse.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.symmetric_point_channel_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.symmetric_point_channel_sum","kind":"theorem","line":8,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/symmetric-point-channel-collapse.lean#L8-L26","doc":"**Channel sum at the symmetric point (division-free core).**  For an\ninvolutive unit (`s² = 1`, the `q = 1` specialisation of the Hecke\nrelation) in any commutative ring, the inverse coincides with the element\nand the unaveraged channel sum is `2s`.  No inverse of `2`, no field:\nthis is the multiplicative-relation (\"R[h]\") form of `(s + s⁻¹)/2 = s`\nper §7c. ","signatureChunk":0}]}